/T (About two-thirds \(64%\) of the household population in Ethiopia has access to electricity and 89% of the household population uses clean fuels or technologies for lighting, such as electricity, solar lanterns, rechargeable flashlights/torches/lanterns, battery-powered flashlights/torches/lanterns, and biogas lamps.)
/E (About two-thirds \(64%\) of the household population in Ethiopia has access to electricity and 89% of the household population uses clean fuels or technologies for lighting, such as electricity, solar lanterns, rechargeable flashlights/torches/lanterns, battery-powered flashlights/torches/lanterns, and biogas lamps.)
