/E (Eleven percent of the household population uses clean fuels and technologies for cooking, including stoves/cookers using electricity, liquefied petroleum gas \(LPG\)/natural gas/biogas, solar, and alcohol/ethanol. The use of clean fuels and technologies for cooking is much higher in urban areas than in rural areas \(34% versus 2%\). )
