/T (More than half \(57%\) of the household population in Ethiopia has access to at least basic drinking water service. At least basic drinking water service includes drinking water from an improved source, either on the premises or with a round-trip collection time of less than 30 minutes. Access to at least basic drinking water service is lowest in Afar \(30%\) and highest in Addis Ababa \(91%\).)
/E (More than half \(57%\) of the household population in Ethiopia has access to at least basic drinking water service. At least basic drinking water service includes drinking water from an improved source, either on the premises or with a round-trip collection time of less than 30 minutes. Access to at least basic drinking water service is lowest in Afar \(30%\) and highest in Addis Ababa \(91%\).)
