/Title (Overall, 11% of children under age 5 had a fever in the  two weeks before the survey. Advice or treatment  was sought for 41% of those children with fever. The most common source of medicine for treating children with fever was government health centres \(20%\), followed by private clinics \(13%\).)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 6572 0 R
/Prev 6579 0 R
/Next 6591 0 R
>>
